  "answer": "File and folder tagging, with metadata stored on the file in the style of macOS, has been requested before. PowerToys#150 is the main tracking issue. Later reports such as #40123 and #18039 were closed as duplicates of it. Nothing has shipped yet. Add your +1 and your points to #150: the openmeta-compatible cross-platform standard, and AI-assisted tagging and sorting like Hazel. Those points are not covered there yet. Commenters on #150 mention existing third-party tools you can use in the meantime: FileMeta, Files, and Folder Marker. They also note a design question that is still open: tags need to live in the file itself (or in desktop.ini or extended attributes) so they survive moves and sharing."
